From c717df11382077a37ee633d4b08329d9e2510164 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:09:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 067/118] tools decode-link: one link, and an exit status
 scripts can tell apart

The command takes one link, as the argument or from the standard input: its
callers read links one at a time. Exit status 0 with the outbound printed and
"warning: ..." lines on the standard error; 2 with one "error: ..." line and
nothing printed when the link cannot be used; 1 for anything else, which is
also what a sing-box without the command answers when called with --compact
(with no flag it prints the help of "tools" with status 0).

A test of the command itself: the previous change crashed it on every valid
xhttp link while the tests of the decoder passed.
